    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully fixed the bug. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## The Problem\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag was not being passed to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI, so the GitHub Actions workflow file wasn't being created.\n\n## The Root Cause\nThe `frai` CLI program defines a `--ci` option at the root level. When commander parsed `frai gate init --ci`, it consumed the `--ci` flag at the program level before it could reach the `gate` subcommand, leaving only `[\"init\"]` in the args array.\n\n## The Solution\nModified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 752-754) to:\n1. Find the index of `'gate'` in `process.argv`\n2. Extract all arguments after `'gate'` directly from `process.argv`\n3. Pass these arguments to the spawned `frai-gate` process\n\nThis ensures all flags (including `--ci`) are preserved and passed through correctly.\n\n## Verification\n\u2705 Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build`\n\u2705 Tested `frai gate init --ci` and confirmed both files are now created:\n   - `FRAI-SPEC.md` \u2713\n   - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` \u2713\n\nThe changes are ready to commit. Would you like me to proceed with creating the git commit?",
